   "key": "total",
   "label": "Total (over/under)",
   "order": 2,
   "why": "Originated second: the total depends on pace and on both scoring rates, which the same model already estimates, but it is priced off a different error process - the margin-vs-total correlation is negative, so a side edge says nothing about the total."
  },
  {
   "key": "moneyline",
   "label": "Moneyline",
   "order": 3,
   "why": "Originated last: the moneyline is a monotone transform of the spread only if you also model the push/tie mass and the vig. It inherits every spread error and adds conversion error, so it is the least defensible of the three until the spread gate has actually been passed."
  }
